an class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Nightly rentals</strong><span class="t">R3 and C3 only</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M16 10h4a2 2 0 0 1 0 4h-4l-4 7H9l2-7H7l-2 2H3l2-4-2-4h2l2 2h4L9 3h3z"/></svg></span><span><strong>Airport</strong><span class="t">15 min drive</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated June 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Nightly rentals are legal only in the R3 and C3 zones along the ocean. A map of both sides, what homes sell for, and what each costs to own.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the Town of Surfside Beach, rentals of under 30 days are allowed only in the R3 and C3 zoning districts, the blocks along the ocean. Those blocks hold 1,662 of the town's 4,045 homes, about 4 in 10.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the inland R1 and R2 streets, a home is for living in or for renting by the year. A house near the ocean sold for about $1 million at the middle in the past year, and an inland house for about $485,000 to $540,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send a listing. We tell you which side of the rental line it is on.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Send us a Surfside listing</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="rental-map"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Rental map">Where are short-term rentals allowed in Surfside Beach?</h2><style>
