e">Atlantic Ocean</text><text class="sm" x="4100" y="1360">Ocean Lakes</text><text class="sm" x="4100" y="1500">(not in the town)</text><g><line x1="260" y1="300" x2="394" y2="165" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="22" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="394" cy="165" r="26" fill="#1c2028"/><text class="sm" x="479" y="120" text-anchor="middle">N</text></g><g><line x1="3543" y1="2448" x2="4348" y2="2448" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="18"/><text class="sm sea" x="3945.5" y="2408" text-anchor="middle">half a mile</text></g></svg></div><figcaption>Where nightly rentals are allowed in the Town of Surfside Beach. Map drawn by Chapter3 from the town's zoning map and Horry County parcel records. Turned so the beach runs along the bottom; the arrow points north.</figcaption><ul class="c3-sb-key" aria-label="Map key"><li><span class="c3-sb-sw" style="background:#d9823b"></span><span><b>R3 and C3: nightly rentals allowed.</b> 1,662 homes.</span></li><li><span class="c3-sb-sw" style="background:#5f9a6e"></span><span><b>R1 and R2: no rentals under 30 days.</b> 1,874 homes.</span></li><li><span class="c3-sb-sw" style="background:#c8c2b8"></span><span><b>Other districts</b> (planned developments and commercial land): we check the parcel. 509 homes.</span></li></ul></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">R1 and R2 cover most of the streets between the band and the commercial strip on US 17 Business. There, the town allows long-term rentals of 365 days or more, and no rentals under 30 days.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town code names those two kinds of rental and nothing in between. Before you plan on renting an inland house by the month in winter, we get the town's answer for that street.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Of the 77 homes we counted for sale inside the town, 45 were on the rental side and 24 on the inland side. The gray planned developments, 447 homes, each have their own approved uses, so we read the approval for the parcel.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the line looks like from the air</h3><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-rental-line-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-rental-line-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-rental-line-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Surfside Beach near the pier, with the inland streets of houses under trees tinted green and labelled No nightly rentals, R1 and R2, and the blocks of beach houses near the ocean tinted orange and labelled Nightly rentals allowed, R3" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Near the pier, from the air. Green: R1 and R2, no rentals under 30 days. Orange: R3, nightly rentals allowed. Tints drawn by Chapter3 from the town's zoning map.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The two sides look different. Near the ocean, tall beach houses stand close together on small lots. Inland, houses sit farther apart under the trees.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Is the house you like on the rental side?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing or the address. We place it on the town's zoning map and tell you which rules apply before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Send us a Surfside listing</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="own-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Its own town">Is Surfside Beach part of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Surfside Beach is its own town in Horry County, incorporated in 1964, with its own council, police department, beach rules and rental zones. Its mailing ZIP code is 29575, and it covers about 1.9 square miles south of Myrtle Beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A "Surfside Beach" address does not prove a home is in the town. Of 231 homes we counted for sale with that address, only 77 were inside the town limits. The other 154, about two in three, are on county land, where the town's rental zones do not apply.</p><div class="c3-sb-note"><b>How the town began.</b> Much of its land was once the Ark Plantation. The beach was later called Roach's Beach, then Floral Beach, and took the name Surfside Beach in 1952. In 1954, Hurricane Hazel destroyed 18 of the 65 houses then at the beach.</div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On Census Day 2020 the town had 4,155 people and 4,317 homes. About 4 in 10 of those homes were held for seasonal or occasional use. Homes in the town are in Horry County Schools, which assigns schools by address; we look up the schools for any home you like.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What do you own at Ocean Lakes?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ocean Lakes Family Campground is next to the town's north end, about 7 minutes from the pier by car, and it is not in the town. It has 2,579 annual lease sites on one 241.67-acre parcel.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At Ocean Lakes you buy the house, mobile home or camper on the site, not the land. Of 956 county tax records there with a building, 949 carry no land value. The middle building is valued at about $248,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The lease terms and the yearly site fee are the campground's. We get them and read them with you before you offer.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Ocean%20Lakes">Ask about a home in Ocean Lakes<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">What do homes cost in Surfside Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house near the ocean costs about twice an inland house. In the past year, R3 houses sold for about $1,000,000 at the middle, and R1 houses for about $540,000.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a home in Surfside Beach sold for in the past year, at the middle"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a home in Surfside Beach sold for in the past year, at the middle</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Side and kind of home, how many sold</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses near the ocean (R3)</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">39 sold, nightly rentals allowed</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,000,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses inland (R1)</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">20 sold, the largest lots</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.542" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$540,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses inland (R2)</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">28 sold</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.487" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$485,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos near the ocean (R3)</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">45 sold, nightly rentals allowed</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.38" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$380,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Every sale Horry County recorded inside the town limits in the 12 months to September 2026.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The two sides are built to different rules. R3 allows buildings up to 55 feet, and a detached house on a lot of 3,600 square feet (3,000 for an attached house). R1 allows 35 feet on 9,000 square feet, and R2 35 feet on 6,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Town-wide, 179 homes sold at a middle price of about $534,000. Of the 175 buyers whose mailing address we could match, 81 lived outside South Carolina.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Asking prices now: the 19 houses for sale on the rental side ask about $1.25 million at the middle, and the 19 inland houses about $545,000. Condos on the rental side ask about $519,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most houses here have no HOA (homeowners association) fee: 36 of the 42 houses listed in the town have none. Our page on <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">homes with no HOA</a> covers what that lets you park and build.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Know what one Surfside Beach home is worth</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We pull the recorded sales on its street and its side of the line, and tell you what they say about the price.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Have us pull the sales for a home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Surfside Beach each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a buyer of an inland R1 house the county values at about $488,000, the middle R1 house, the town and county tax as a main home is about $2,050 a year, before credits. With the middle inland flood policy, if you insure for flood (about $700), that is about $2,750 a year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That is besides the mortgage and home insurance. Owners who bought years ago often pay less tax because of the state's 15 percent cap on reassessment.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Main home or rental: about 3 times the tax</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina taxes your main home on 4 percent of its value, and it skips the school operating tax. A second home or rental is taxed on 6 percent and pays all of it. Inside the town the 2026 rate is 214.2 mills.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">A home the county values at $500,000</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Town and county tax a year, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Your main home</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$2,100</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A second home or rental</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$6,400</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before credits and the 15 percent cap. The 214.2 mills are 52.1 county, 119.1 school (109.1 of it school operations) and 43.0 town. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax calculator</a> has every town's rate.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Flood insurance near the ocean and inland</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the south town line to the pier, where two in three town homes are R3 or C3, a single-family flood policy costs a middle $1,256 a year. In an inland part of town where 9 in 10 homes are R1 or R2, it costs $702.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">FEMA rates the town Class 7 in its Community Rating System, which takes 15 percent off flood insurance here. The county land around the town is rated Class 5.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the yearly cost of one address</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We work out its tax as a main home and as a rental, and get a flood quote for the house.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Have us work out the tax on an address</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="daily-life"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Daily life">What is everyday life like in Surfside Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every home in the town is within about 0.8 mile of Ocean Boulevard, the beach road, in a straight line. Even on the inland R1 streets, no home is more than 0.65 mile from it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The concrete pier</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town's fishing pier is 814 feet long, 25 feet tall and all concrete. It opened on March 14, 2024, on the town's 60th birthday. Walking on it is free.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the Surfside Beach Pier, labelled, running from a wide beach into a green ocean, with parking lots and rows of beach houses behind the sand" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>The concrete pier from the air, with the beach parking lots and the streets of beach houses behind it.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It has two restaurants, The Whistling Duck and Surf Diner, an ice cream shop and a bait shop. A day of fishing is $14. From April through October it is open from 6 a.m. to 1 a.m.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The beach, parking and the rules</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town has 36 public beach accesses and 12 beach parking lots. Five accesses have wheelchair access, and beach wheelchairs are available through the town police department.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A row of two- and three-story beach houses in blue, yellow and gray behind low dunes, seen across a wide sand beach under a blue sky at Surfside Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: BullDawg2021. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: BullDawg2021</a></span></div><figcaption>Beach houses behind the dunes at Surfside Beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An owner who lives elsewhere gets two free parking passes for town lots per household, and $40 buys each extra one. Everyone else pays from March 1 to October 31, 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.: $2 or $3 an hour at most lots, $4 at the pier lot.</p><ul class="c3-sb-rules"><li><strong>Dogs</strong>Off the beach from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day. Leashed dogs are welcome at other times. No pets on the pier.</li><li><strong>Golf carts</strong>On town streets with a state permit, never on the sand.</li><li><strong>Fires and grills</strong>None on the beach, and no smoking on the beach or the accesses.</li><li><strong>Shade</strong>Tents and canopies up to 10 by 10 feet.</li><li><strong>Boats</strong>Launch only at the 4th Avenue South access.</li><li><strong>Jet skis</strong>At least 150 yards out from May 15 to September 15.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Golf carts</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most trips here need a car or a golf cart. To drive one on the street, South Carolina law requires a DMV permit decal and registration, liability insurance, and a licensed driver 16 or older.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The decal costs $5 and is replaced every five years, or when you move. Carts may use only roads posted at 35 mph or less. A cart driven at night must have working headlights and taillights.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town council passed its own golf cart ordinance, 25-0990, on August 26, 2025, by 5 votes to 2. Speakers at the meeting argued for and against a 24-hour rule. We get the ordinance's current hours from the town for you.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is everything?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Drive times by car from the pier, without traffic. Summer traffic on US 17 Business is slower.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From the Surfside Beach Pier to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Food Lion on US 17 Business</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">5 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Garden City Pier</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach State Park</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">11 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">12 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The MarshWalk in Murrells Inlet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">12 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Market Common</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">14 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Coastal Grand Mall</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Huntington Beach State Park</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Grand Strand Medical Center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">25 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Surfside Beach flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inland, very little of it is in a high-risk zone: 2 percent of R2 homes and 16 percent of R1 homes. Near the ocean it is most homes: 78 percent in R3, and every home on the ocean side of Ocean Boulevard.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, by side of the rental line"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, by side of the rental line</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where</span><span role="columnheader">Share of homes</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Inland, R2</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.02" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">2 percent</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Inland, R1</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.155" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">16 percent</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The whole town</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.39" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">39 percent</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Near the ocean, R3</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.783" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">78 percent</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>FEMA flood zones AE and VE on Horry County's flood map, at each home's parcel.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Town-wide, 39 percent of homes are in a high-risk zone, where a lender requires flood insurance.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The 48 percent rule</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This town rule matters most for an older, low house. If repairs or improvements to a building whose lowest floor is below the 100-year flood level cost 48 percent or more of the building's value, the whole building must be raised to that level plus 3 feet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town uses the county assessor's building value, land excluded, unless the owner submits a licensed appraisal. The middle home in the town was built in about 1985.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you offer on an older house near the ocean, we pull its flood zone and the county's building value. You then know how much work the rule allows before the house must be raised.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the storms did</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pier was first built in 1953. Hurricane Hazel destroyed it in 1954 and Hurricane Hugo in 1989, and it was not rebuilt until 1993. Hurricane Matthew in 2016 took more than half of its length.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/invest-where-to-buy/surfside-beach-pier-and-houses-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/invest-where-to-buy/surfside-beach-pier-and-houses-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/invest-where-to-buy/surfside-beach-pier-and-houses-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="675" alt="The Surfside Beach fishing pier with a parking lot on one side and rows of raised beach houses on the other, seen from over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="USGS photo, 2011. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">USGS photo, 2011</a></span></div><figcaption>The old wooden pier and the raised beach houses beside it, seen from a plane in 2011. Hurricane Matthew took more than half of this pier in 2016.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Near the ocean the town is in hurricane evacuation Zone A. Part of it east of US 17 Business, from 16th Avenue North to Vista Drive, is in Zone B. The zone goes by address.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our pages on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">finding out whether a house has flooded</a> and <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance</a> show what else we look at.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the flood facts for one Surfside Beach house</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We pull its flood zone and the county's building value, and tell you where the 48 percent line falls.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Have us check a house for flooding</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="airbnb"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting it out">Can you Airbnb a house in Surfside Beach, and what does it earn?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, in R3 and C3, with a town business licence for each rental property. Stays under 90 days also owe the town's 1 percent hospitality fee and 0.5 percent local accommodations tax. You report them each month, or every 28 days, even if you rent only once or twice a year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Guests pay about 12 percent in lodging taxes on top of the rent: 9 percent collected by the state, the county's 1.5 percent and the town's 1.5 percent. You collect it and send it on, so it is not income.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What a Surfside Beach area rental earns</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">AirROI, a rental data company, tracks the short-term rentals in its Surfside Beach market. Over the past 12 months:</p><ul class="c3-sb-stats" aria-label="Short-term rental numbers for the Surfside Beach area, past 12 months"><li><b>$42,902</b><span>the average listing's gross bookings in a year</span></li><li><b>37%</b><span>of nights booked</span></li><li><b>$419</b><span>average nightly rate</span></li><li><b>551</b><span>active listings</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The average listing's bookings rose 7.1 percent on the year before. Most of the money comes in summer: the average listing takes in about $11,600 in July and $2,360 in January, about five times as much.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a Surfside Beach area rental takes in, in a typical month"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a Surfside Beach area rental takes in, in a typical month</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Listings</span><span role="columnheader">Gross bookings a month</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Bottom quarter of listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.141" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,810 or less</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The middle listing</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.3" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$3,840</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Top quarter</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.584" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$7,470 or more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Top tenth</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$12,800 or more</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>AirROI, every active Airbnb and Vrbo listing in its Surfside Beach market, before cleaning, fees and management.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Worked example: a condo near the ocean, rented by the night</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take the middle R3 condo that sold in the past year, about $380,000, and say it books what the average listing here books. No loan is in this example.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">One year of nightly renting</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">About</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Gross bookings, the average listing in AirROI's area</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$42,902</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Less town and county tax at 6 percent, if the county values it at the price paid</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$4,880</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Left for dues, cleaning, management, insurance and utilities</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$38,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">AirROI's figure covers every kind of rental in its area, houses and condos together. Condo dues, the building's flood share and management depend on the building, so we price them for the exact unit before you offer.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Thinking of renting a Surfside condo or house by the night?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We confirm it is in R3 or C3, and price the tax, the dues and the insurance for that unit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Ask about renting a Surfside home</a></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Renting by the year is allowed in every district with homes. To compare towns, <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">compare all nine submarkets</a>. The rules by town are on our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a>, and the yearly rental math on our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">long-term rental page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="pros-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Surfside Beach?</h2><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Every home is within about 0.8 mile of the beach road.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A new concrete pier, free to walk, with two restaurants.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Owners who live elsewhere park free with two town passes.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Its own police, beach rules and a map of where you may rent.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>On the R3 side, about 1 home in 8 is taxed as its owner's main home. <span class="c3-pc-do">For year-round streets, look inland: in R1, 71 percent are main homes.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Flood insurance costs more near the ocean, and the 48 percent rule limits work on low houses. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the zone and the building value first.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Two in three "Surfside Beach" listings are outside the town. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the town limits for every listing.</span></span></li></ul></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Comparing beach towns? Our guides to <a href="/submarkets/garden-city/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Garden City</a>, just south, <a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Murrells Inlet</a> and <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach</a> cover their own rules and prices.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="surfside-beach-sc-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Surfside Beach, SC FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Surfside Beach part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Surfside Beach is its own town in Horry County, incorporated in 1964, with the ZIP code 29575.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you Airbnb in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only in the R3 and C3 zoning districts, the blocks along the ocean. Rentals under 30 days are not allowed in R1 or R2.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you drive a golf cart in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, on town streets posted at 35 mph or less, with a state permit decal, insurance and a licensed driver 16 or older. Never on the beach.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are dogs allowed on Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day. At other times, leashed dogs are welcome.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is parking free in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Town lots charge from March 1 to October 31, 8 a.m. to 6 p.m. An owner who lives elsewhere gets two free passes per household.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax rate in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the town it is 214.2 mills, on 4 percent of the value for a main home and 6 percent for a second home or rental.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What schools serve Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Schools, which assigns schools by address. We look up the schools for any home you like.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Surfside Beach safe?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. The town has its own police department, and reported crime by agency is public at the FBI Crime Data Explorer.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://library.municode.com/sc/surfside_beach/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=CH17ZO" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Town Code 17-396.10</a>, <a href="https://surfsidebeach.org/DocumentCenter/View/3026/New-Zoning-Map" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town zoning map</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFEMA policies</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/DocumentCenter/View/392/48-Percent-Rule-PDF" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">48 percent rule</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/212/Surfside-Beach-Fishing-Pier" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the pier</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/200/Beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town beaches</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/202/Parking" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">parking</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t56c002.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 56-2</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_08262025-1302" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">council minutes</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/DocumentCenter/View/148" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">business licence guide</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST575.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR ST-575</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/surfside-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI</a>, <a href="https://www.oceanlakes.com/lodging-2/annual-lease-sales/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ocean Lakes</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table?g=160XX00US4570585" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census 2020</a>. Our counts: the town's zoning map traced onto county parcels, flood maps and deeds. Listings counted in aggregate. Not legal or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Near the pier, from the air. Green: R1 and R2, no rentals under 30 days. Orange: R3, nightly rentals allowed. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from one NOAA aerial photo, resized it, adjusted the colors, tinted the zoning districts and added labels.</div><div role="listitem">The concrete pier from the air, with the beach parking lots and the streets of beach houses behind it. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from one NOAA aerial photo, resized it, adjusted the colors and added a label.</div><div role="listitem">Beach houses along the sand at Surfside Beach. Photo: BullDawg2021, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surfside_Beach_Shoreline.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">The pier and rows of raised beach houses in Surfside Beach. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps t