"pb-16">   <section id="overview" class="mg-col pt-16 sm:pt-20"> <div class="mg-title mb-8"> <p class="font-lato text-[12px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]"> The short answer </p> <h2 class="mg-serif mt-1.5 text-[30px] font-bold leading-[1.12] sm:text-[36px] tracking-[-0.012em] text-[#1e293b]"> Surfside Beach Airbnb Market at a Glance </h2>  </div> <div class="mg-prose"> <p id="introduction-earning-shape">Rates in Surfside Beach run ahead of the South Carolina average, with bookings close to it. Listings averaged <strong>$419</strong> a night and were booked on <strong>37%</strong> of available nights, against $355 and 39% for the South Carolina average.</p><p id="introduction-seasonality">Timing matters: in <strong>July</strong>, usually the best month, the average listing earns about five times as much as in <strong>January</strong>, usually the slowest.</p><p id="introduction-market-context">With 551 active listings, Surfside Beach is the 11th-largest of 116 South Carolina markets AirROI tracks. From a year earlier, average revenue rose 7% while the number of active listings grew 24%.</p> </div> <a href="/atlas/map?country-code=US&#38;state=South-Carolina&#38;city=Surfside-Beach" rel="nofollow" class="pseo-atlas group relative block min-h-[76px] overflow-hidden rounded-[4px] font-lato mt-8"> <img src="https://airroi.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/public/assets/cities/United%20States/South%20Carolina/Surfside%20Beach.png" alt="Map of Airbnb listings in Surfside Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"> <span class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-950/85 via-slate-900/55 to-slate-900/20"></span> <span class="relative flex min-h-[76px] items-center px-5 py-3 text-white"> <span class="flex-1"> <span class="block text-[15px] font-bold">Browse the live Surfside Beach Airbnb market</span> <span class="mt-0.5 hidden text-[12.5px] text-slate-300 sm:block">Search by revenue, occupancy and neighborhood on an interactive map</span> </span> <span class="ml-3 inline-flex shrink-0 items-center rounded-[4px] bg-white px-3.5 py-1.5 text-[13px] font-bold text-[#1e293b]">
+See Every Surfside Beach Listing
+</span> </span> </a> </section> <section id="revenue" class="mg-section mg-col"> <div class="mg-title mb-8"> <p class="font-lato text-[12px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]"> Revenue </p> <h2 class="mg-serif mt-1.5 text-[30px] font-bold leading-[1.12] sm:text-[36px] tracking-[-0.012em] text-[#1e293b]"> How Much Do Airbnb Hosts Make in Surfside Beach? </h2>  </div> <div class="mg-report prose max-w-none"> <p id="revenue-summary">Gross bookings per Surfside Beach listing averaged <strong>$42,902</strong> over the 12 months to September 2026 (South Carolina average: $37,525), before cleaning, platform and management costs and taxes.</p><div id="monthly-revenue"> <p>In a typical year, the average Surfside Beach listing brings in <strong>$11,600</strong> in July, its best month, and <strong>$2,360</strong> in January, its slowest. The three strongest months bring in 46% of a full year's revenue, where an even calendar would give any three months 25%.</p><p>In a typical month, a top-quarter listing earns at least 4.1 times as much as a bottom-quarter one.</p><ul class="not-prose my-5 space-y-1.5"><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#0d47a1"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Best-in-class properties</span> (top 10%) earn <strong>$12,800+</strong> a month, about 3.3 times the typical property.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#1976d2"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Strong performers</span> (top 25%) earn <strong>$7,470</strong> or more, roughly $3,600 a month above the median.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#64b5f6"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Typical properties</span> (median) earn about <strong>$3,840</strong> a month.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#bbdefb"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Entry-level properties</span> (bottom 25%) earn <strong>$1,810</strong> or less, about half of the median.</li></ul><p class="not-prose my-4 font-lato text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]">
+These are monthly figures for listings active in each month. The annual average above also counts listings
+            that operated for only part of the year, so it runs below twelve times these figures.
